    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This paper investigates the role of the Brazilian Municipal Education Plans (PMEs) in shaping local educational policies. The study evaluates the alignment of Municipal Education Plans with national guidelines and how they are effectively used to shape education policies at the municipal level. Using a case study methodology, the research focuses on two Brazilian states, Amapá and Ceará, analyzing thirty municipal plans and conducting eleven semi-structured interviews with policymakers. Findings reveal significant disparities in the Municipal Education Plans, with many plans lacking specific, context-sensitive strategies and adequate monitoring mechanisms. The study highlights that municipalities do not refer to plans in their daily activities. Also, federal resources appear to be a more significant driver of municipal actions than the plans themselves. The results indicate the need for enhanced federal support and capacity-building measures to ensure adequate educational planning and implementation at the municipal level.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Almeida, A. (2024). Municipal Education Plans in Brazil: How They Shape Local Policies. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/jp693zr6293. https://doi.org/10.25740/jp693zr6293.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
